# The golden baselines of AWSCognitoAuthPlugin, the tests that pin them and the lock that guards them
# require admin approval. GoldenTests/ is owned whole, so every golden test and what decides its verdict
# (GoldenFileSupport.swift, LogTranscriptNormaliser.swift, ErrorCatalogueConstants.swift, the fixture
# paths each test reads) needs an admin, including files added there later. So does the plugin's shared
# scheme: CI tests through it, and its launch environment can set AMPLIFY_GENERATE_GOLDEN, which makes
# the golden tests write their files instead of comparing them. GoldenGenerateModeGuardTests fails a
# full-scheme run with that switch set however it got in (scheme, TEST_RUNNER_, shell), so the scheme
# rule is a backstop. These close only the generate switch: skipping or deselecting the golden suites
# through the CI workflows or scripts/python/ stays a team-reviewed change.
/AmplifyPlugins/Auth/Tests/AWSCognitoAuthPluginUnitTests/TestResources/GoldenStoredFormat/ @aws-amplify/amplify-ios-admins
/AmplifyPlugins/Auth/Tests/AWSCognitoAuthPluginUnitTests/TestResources/GoldenErrors/ @aws-amplify/amplify-ios-admins
/AmplifyPlugins/Auth/Tests/AWSCognitoAuthPluginUnitTests/TestResources/GoldenLogs/ @aws-amplify/amplify-ios-admins
/AmplifyPlugins/Auth/Tests/AWSCognitoAuthPluginUnitTests/TestResources/GoldenKeychainQueries/ @aws-amplify/amplify-ios-admins
/AmplifyPlugins/Auth/Tests/AWSCognitoAuthPluginUnitTests/TestResources/GoldenConfiguration/ @aws-amplify/amplify-ios-admins
/AmplifyPlugins/Auth/Tests/AWSCognitoAuthPluginUnitTests/GoldenTests/ @aws-amplify/amplify-ios-admins
/.swiftpm/xcode/xcshareddata/xcschemes/AWSCognitoAuthPlugin.xcscheme @aws-amplify/amplify-ios-admins
/.github/workflows/auth_golden_fixture_lock.yml @aws-amplify/amplify-ios-admins

# The shared Cognito module's gates and their inputs require admin approval, so a team-approved change
# cannot weaken a check and pass it together. scripts/cognito-engine/ is owned whole:
# - check_fixture_lock.sh: the golden-fixture lock above.
# - check_engine_deps.py: no Amplify dependency or import reaches the module that AmplifyCognitoClient uses.
# - check_engine_privacy_manifest.py: no product that links the module misses a required-reason declaration.
# - error_match_gate.sh: no `catch`, cast or type test against an error type the module no longer throws,
#   which would compile and silently never match.
# - gen_engine_paths.py, gen_error_constants_list.py, rename_table.json: inputs of those gates and of the
#   error and log golden tests (the log normaliser reads rename_table.json).
/scripts/cognito-engine/ @aws-amplify/amplify-ios-admins
/.github/workflows/auth_engine_gates.yml @aws-amplify/amplify-ios-admins
# engine_paths.txt is the exception (the last matching rule wins). It changes whenever a file of the module
# is added, removed or renamed, CI checks it against gen_engine_paths.py (admin-owned above), and
# error_match_gate.sh treats every file under the module's Sources/ as module code whether listed or not.
/scripts/cognito-engine/engine_paths.txt @aws-amplify/amplify-ios
